Subject: Menu: the level screenshots and minimaps loaded when a level is shown

loadLevel loaded every level's screenshot and minimap at the start, for
the menu's level screens: about 190 levels (the single races and the
events' own), some 380 pictures of 256x256, about 127 MB of textures with
their mipmaps, decoded before the menu shows. On the PS3 that filled the
GPU's memory, so the race's own textures (the car, the sky, the
buildings) failed to allocate and the race drew without them.

loadLevel now keeps the paths. The two level screens load their level's
pair when they show it (MainApp::menuThumb: the same texture, mipmapped,
as before), and the previous level's pair is freed; starting a race frees
it too. Nothing else used the pictures (the race's map is the terrain's
own HUD map). A level without a picture, or one that fails to load,
shows the "no screenshot" / "no minimap" picture, as before.

Forwarded: not-needed

